---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ProductGrid from '../../components/ProductGrid.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/quote/QuoteForm.tsx';
import { serviceSchema } from '../../lib/schema/service';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema/faqPage';
import { getAllProducts } from '../../data/catalog/shopify';
import '../../styles/quote-form.css';

const allProducts = await getAllProducts();
const products = allProducts.filter((p) => p.tags.includes('garland')).slice(0, 9);

const faqs = (await getCollection('faq'))
  .filter((f) => f.data.pages.includes('garlands'))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .map((f) => ({ question: f.data.question, body: f.body.trim() }));

const schemas = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Balloon garlands',
    description:
      'Custom organic balloon garlands built to length and colour palette, delivered and installed for events in London Ontario.',
    startingPrice: 160,
    url: '/services/balloon-garlands',
  }),
];
if (faqs.length > 0) {
  schemas.push(faqPageSchema(faqs.map((f) => ({ question: f.question, answer: f.body }))));
}
---

<BaseLayout
  topic="Balloon Garlands"
  description="Custom balloon garlands in London Ontario. Built to your length, colours, and surface, then delivered and installed. Accent garlands from $160, full feature walls to $1,200."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services' },
    { name: 'Balloon garlands', url: '/services/balloon-garlands' },
  ]}
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Install type"
    headline="Balloon garlands in London, Ontario"
    subhead="Organic garlands built to your length and palette. Wrapped along rails, draped across head tables, climbing a feature wall."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/quote', label: 'Start a quote' }}
    secondaryCta={{ href: '/portfolio', label: 'See garland work' }}
    image="/images/categories/SpringFloralBalloonGarland.webp"
    imageAlt="Spring floral balloon garland in soft pastel tones"
    variant="page"
  />

  <section class="install-body section">
    <div class="container container-narrow prose">
      <p>
        A garland works as a single accent piece or as the structural base for something much larger. It
        is the most adaptable thing we build, because it takes the shape of whatever surface it goes on
        rather than imposing one.
      </p>

      <h2>What a balloon garland costs in London</h2>
      <p>
        Small accent garlands for a table run, a dessert display, or a backdrop corner start around
        $160. A standard eight to twelve foot garland for a shower, birthday, or office event runs $200
        to $500. Large organic garlands covering a staircase, spanning a head table, or climbing a full
        feature wall land between $700 and $1,200.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three things move that number. Length is the obvious one. Colour count matters more than people
        expect, since every added colour is a separate inflation batch and a separate sort before the
        build starts. And the surface decides the method, because brick, glass, and anything a venue
        will not let us drill into each need a different approach to hold weight safely.
      </p>

      <h2>Where garlands actually go</h2>
      <p>
        Along a stair rail is the classic, and it photographs well because the curve of the stairs does
        half the work. Across the front of a head table or a dessert table adds height at eye level
        without taking up the surface. Around a doorway or window frame turns an ordinary opening into
        something intentional. Up one corner and along a ceiling line gives a room scale for far less
        than a full <a href="/services/ceiling">ceiling install</a>. And wrapped around the edge of a
        backdrop, a garland softens the join between the wall and the room.
      </p>
      <p>
        For venues that permit nothing on the walls, garlands can be built onto a freestanding frame
        instead, which costs a little more but keeps the option open. Tell us the venue and we will
        confirm what is allowed there before quoting.
      </p>

      <h2>Indoors, outdoors, and how long they last</h2>
      <p>
        Garlands are air-filled rather than helium, which is why they hold their shape for days or weeks
        instead of hours. Indoors they comfortably outlast the event, and installs set up the night
        before are normal. Outdoors, direct summer sun is the limit. Sun oxidizes latex to a chalky
        matte finish within hours and heat expands the air enough that balloons in full sun can pop, so
        for outdoor work we underinflate slightly, favour shade, and set up closer to the start time.
        The <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> covers outdoor durability in more detail.
      </p>

      <h2>Related install types</h2>
      <p>
        Need something that frames a doorway or a ceremony to walk under? That is a
        <a href="/services/balloon-arches">balloon arch</a>. Want a solid photo background rather than a
        trailing accent? See <a href="/services/walls-backdrops">walls and backdrops</a>. A garland
        trailing off one corner of a wall is one of the most requested combinations we build.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {products.length > 0 && (
    <section class="install-products section">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Shop the catalog</p>
          <h2>Balloon garlands in the catalog</h2>
          <p class="lede">Pick a build as-is or use one as the starting point for a custom version.</p>
        </header>
        <ProductGrid products={products} columns={3} />
        <p class="section-link-wrap">
          <a class="section-link" href="https://shop.balloonia.events/collections/arches-garlands">View all garlands →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  {faqs.length > 0 && <FAQAccordion heading="Balloon garland questions" faqs={faqs} />}

  <section class="install-quote section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Custom build</p>
        <h2>Need something specific?</h2>
        <p class="lede">Send the wall or table you want covered, your colours, and your date.</p>
      </header>
      <QuoteForm client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: var(--line-relaxed);
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .section-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .install-quote {
    background: var(--color-paper-soft);
  }
  .section-link {
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .section-link-wrap {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
